From: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 16:03:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: fix EDMA RX DMA direction

EDMA RX fill buffers are written by the device, but both the linear and
page-mode allocation paths map them with DMA_TO_DEVICE. Their reap paths
already unmap with DMA_FROM_DEVICE, exposing the mismatch on non-coherent
systems.

Map both receive buffer forms with DMA_FROM_DEVICE.

Signed-off-by: VKing <noreply@openwrt.local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_rx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/edma_rx.c
@@ -68 +68 @@
-			buff_addr = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, dma_map_size, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			buff_addr = dma_map_single(dev, skb->data, dma_map_size, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
@@ -87 +87 @@
-			buff_addr = dma_map_page(dev, pg, 0, PAGE_SIZE, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
+			buff_addr = dma_map_page(dev, pg, 0, PAGE_SIZE, DMA_FROM_DEVICE);
